"The giants were once people: kidnapped, cursed and dumped in the dungeon to fight."
"Their broken words seem to be remnants of names and speech they had before the curse."
"Some underground monsters are failed summons, but the giants are cursed captives, not animals."
"Giant cores feel wrong, a heavy weight, to one who absorbs them; they hold echoes of the dead."
"Asked, the giant cores answered with pulses, strongest when asked to help fight the arena."
"Only with that consent were the giant cores fused and affixed, into the Eternal Cavedweller Core."
